        "heading_QRfGKH": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Why You Should Use Directional-Flow Tapes for Social Distancing",
            "highlight_style": "none",
            "highlight_font_style": "italic",
            "highlight_style_color": "",
            "highlight_text_color": "",
            "heading_size": "h2"
          }
        },
        "text_R3Jnnb": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>In the fight against the COVID-19 pandemic and other similar crises, one of the greatest defensive weapons is social distancing. This preventative strategy allows public figures and private citizens to help stop the spread of pathogens, reducing the number of affected people and, consequently, the strain on the healthcare system. While social isolation (i.e., completely separating oneself from others) would likely be more effective than social distancing at minimizing or eliminating transmission rates, it is not a sustainable solution since day-to-day activities (e.g., working and food shopping) are still essential.</p><p>In essential businesses where contact with others is largely unavoidable (e.g., banks, grocery stores, and warehouses), many facility owners and managers are implementing social distancing measures to prevent unnecessary or excessive contact between people. For example, they are applying directional-flow social distancing floor decals in their facilities to help employees and customers comply with social distancing guidelines (i.e., maintaining a minimum of six feet of distance whenever possible).</p><p>The following blog post provides an overview of directional-flow tapes, outlining what they are, the benefits they offer for social distancing applications, and the product capabilities available at NADCO.</p>",
            "subtext_color": true
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "subheading_nkTfzr",
        "heading_QRfGKH",
        "text_R3Jnnb"
      ],
