    "image_with_text_dRkCWb": {
      "type": "image-with-text",
      "blocks": {
        "heading_rdA33p": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "What Are Directional-Flow Tapes?",
            "highlight_style": "none",
            "highlight_font_style": "italic",
            "highlight_style_color": "",
            "highlight_text_color": "",
            "heading_size": "hd2"
          }
        },
        "text_xcJE7W": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<h2></h2><p>As suggested by the name, directional-flow tapes are used to guide the flow of foot traffic. They typically feature directional arrows and/or text (e.g., “ENTER,” “EXIT,” or “ONE WAY”). They are designed to be placed on facility floors and positioned to indicate the direction traffic should proceed. For example, in grocery stores, they show customers where to enter, how to move through the store, and where to exit.</p><h2>Benefits of Using Directional-Flow Tapes for Social Distancing Applications</h2><p>The recent global outbreak of COVID-19 has increased the importance of directional-flow tape. Its main functions are maintaining order and organization within a facility and marking out clear paths for customers—both of which help enforce social distancing by keeping foot traffic separated and moving. When used properly, these tapes can contribute to lower transmission rates and safer conditions for employees and customers.</p>",
            "subtext_color": true
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "heading_rdA33p",
        "text_xcJE7W"
      ],
