    "rich_text_nB69mq": {
      "type": "rich-text",
      "blocks": {
        "heading_8tLrX8": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Directional-Flow Tapes From NADCO",
            "highlight_style": "none",
            "highlight_font_style": "italic",
            "highlight_style_color": "",
            "highlight_text_color": "",
            "heading_size": "h2"
          }
        },
        "text_wqtR3t": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>At <strong>NADCO® Tape & Labels</strong>, we specialize in the design, manufacture, and delivery of custom pressure-sensitive tapes and labels. Equipped with more than three decades of industry experience and a state-of-the-art manufacturing facility, we have the expertise to produce adhesive tapes, labels, and other products for nearly any customer need. One of our core product offerings is directional-flow arrow tape, which currently plays a critical role in the fight against COVID-19.</p><p>Our directional-flow tape features an arrow indicating the direction of flow. It is made from a unique combination of liner and overlamination materials that protects it against harsh facility conditions (e.g., heat and cold). Material options include aluminum, cloth, copper foil, foam, paper, polypropylene film, PVC film, and vinyl. It is available in several standard colors and sizes (all compliant with OSHA/ANSI requirements) and is completely customizable to meet highly specific customer needs. While it is generally used on piping to indicate the flow of material, it can also be applied to facility floors to organize and control the flow of traffic for better compliance with social distancing guidelines.</p><p><a href=\"/pages/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"Contact us\"><strong>Contact us today</strong></a> to learn more about our directional-flow tapes and how they can benefit your facility!</p>",
            "text_size": "text-base",
            "text_line_limit": "none",
            "button_style": "btn--underline",
            "button_icon": "none"
          }
        }
      },
